  id: uranus
  title: Uranus
  subtitle: THE SIDEWAYS ICE GIANT
  paragraph: Uranus rolls around the Sun on its side, tipped by about ninety-eight degrees, most likely knocked over long ago by a collision. Each pole spends roughly forty-two years in sunlight and forty-two in darkness. Methane in its atmosphere absorbs red light and leaves it pale blue-green.
